INSERT FOOD ITEMS

As a user of the CoolManager system,
I want to be able to insert food items into the refrigerator,
So that I can store groceries and maintain their freshness.

FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

Manual Door Operation

The CoolManager system does not control the physical opening and closing of the refrigerator door. It is assumed that the user will handle these actions.
Inventory Management

The system should allow the user to manually input the food items placed inside the refrigerator.
Door Status Monitoring

The system should monitor the status of the refrigerator door (open/closed).
Notifications

The system should notify the user if the refrigerator door is left open to ensure food preservation.

USE CASE: INSERT FOOD ITEMS

Primary Actor: User

Preconditions:

The user is logged into the CoolManager system.

Main Success Scenario:

The user opens the refrigerator door manually.
The user places food items inside the refrigerator.
The user manually closes the refrigerator door.
The CoolManager system detects that the door is closed and updates the door status.

Alternate Scenario:

If the door is not closed properly:

The CoolManager system detects the door is still open.
The system sends a notification/reminder to the user to close the door properly.

FUNCTIONAL COMPONENTS

Food Item Entry Interface

Provide an interface where users can input details of food items being stored (e.g., item name, quantity, expiration date).

Door Status Sensor Integration

Integrate with sensors to monitor the refrigerator door status.
Ensure real-time updates of the door status in the system.

Notification System

Implement a notification system to alert the user if the refrigerator door remains open.

USER EXPERIENCE FLOW

Open Door

User manually opens the refrigerator door.

Insert Items

User manually places food items inside the refrigerator.

Close Door

User manually closes the refrigerator door.
Door status sensor detects the door closure.
Confirm Closure

CoolManager system confirms the door is securely closed.
If the door is not closed, the system sends a notification to the user.

ASSUMPTIONS AND DEPENDENCIES

The refrigerator is equipped with sensors that can communicate with the CoolManager system to detect the door status.
The user has access to a device (e.g., smartphone, tablet) to receive notifications from the CoolManager system.
The user is responsible for manually entering the food items into the system.
